            "base_type": "subworkflow",
            "properties": {
              "continue_on_failure": false,
              "description": "**Cisco Meraki - Networks - Create Network**\n\nCreate a network in Meraki Organization. To create a combined network, select more than one Product Types task will automatically create the network as combined type.\n\n**Target:** A Meraki Endpoint using HTTPS \"api.meraki.com\" port 443 and no path.\n\n**Account Key:** Meraki User API Key. API Key can be generated from Meraki Dashboard -\u003e User Profile -\u003e API Access.\n\nSteps:\n[] Sends Create Network request to Meraki\n[] Check if the request was successful:\n[]\u003e If it was, attempt to extract the results and set the output variables\n[]\u003e If it wasn't, check if \"Ignore If Exits\" input is set to true.\n[]\u003e\u003e If it was, skips the \"name already exits\" error and marks the workflow as completed successfully.\n[]\u003e\u003e If it wasn't, return the error and marks the workflow as failed.\n\nNOTE: Empty attributes in the request are removed from the payload before sending to Meraki. \n\nMore information about this API: https://developer.cisco.com/meraki/api-v1/create-organization-network/",
              "display_name": "Meraki - Create Organization Network",
              "input": {
                "variable_workflow_02JJPT9HBQPQ60olVVxRFCRUe38ZJHZw7G0": "$workflow.definition_workflow_02PC4BNZI276Z0CS3bVcKgcro02lsQs09hi.input.variable_workflow_02PC4SI4FW3393Rw7H8ccHQX7l1BgWviAg5$",
